  "id": "rem-sleep-deprivation",
  "term": "REM-sleep deprivation",
  "definition": "REM-sleep deprivation is the prevention or loss of rapid eye movement (REM) sleep. In the source packet, prolonged REM-sleep deprivation in rats is described as a stressful state that raises corticosterone and is typically followed by a rebound increase in REM sleep during recovery.",
